# Architecture

## Monorepo Structure

Stride is a TypeScript monorepo (pnpm) with a strict unidirectional dependency graph:

```
@stridetime/types  →  @stridetime/db  →  @stridetime/core  →  stride-desktop
   (types only)        (schema, repos)    (services, logic)    (UI, pages)
```

**Pending rename (SD-162):** `@stridetime/db` will be renamed to `@stridetime/sync` — same package, same position in the dependency chain, same responsibilities. All current code uses `@stridetime/db`. Once SD-162 is complete, update all import references in these rules and the codebase.

Each layer may only import from layers to its left. Never import upward.

## What Each Layer Contains

| Package | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `@stridetime/types` | Domain types, enums, input interfaces — no logic, no DB |
| `@stridetime/db` | Drizzle schema, repository classes, DB utilities, PowerSync connector (`src/db/connector.ts`). Will be renamed to `@stridetime/sync` via SD-162; will also house `powersync.yaml` after SD-229. |
| `@stridetime/core` | Business logic services, validation, orchestration |
| `stride-desktop` | Tauri + React UI, pages, components, hooks, contexts |
| `stride-mobile` | Expo + React Native — same layer as stride-desktop |
| `stride-admin` | Vite + React admin UI — same layer as stride-desktop |
| `@stridetime/ui` | Shared component library — no business logic |

## Import Rules by Package

### `@stridetime/types`
- Imports from: nothing (leaf node)
- Never imports from any other `@stridetime/*` package

### `@stridetime/db` (future: `@stridetime/sync`)
- Imports from: `@stridetime/types` only
- Never imports from `@stridetime/core` or `stride-desktop`

### `@stridetime/core`
- Imports from: `@stridetime/db` and `@stridetime/types`
- Never imports from `stride-desktop`

### `stride-desktop`
- Imports from: `@stridetime/core` and `@stridetime/types`
- **Never imports from `@stridetime/db`** — the only exception is `src/lib/db.ts` for database initialization

## Service Layer Boundary

- All **mutations** go through services in `@stridetime/core`
- UI components call service methods — never call repository methods directly
- **Reads** use `useQuery` from `@powersync/react` with raw SQL
- **Writes** use service methods

## Key Architectural Decisions

- SQLite (Drizzle ORM) with PowerSync for offline-first sync
- Tauri 2 (Rust) for desktop shell — Rust code lives in `stride-desktop/src-tauri/`
- Every table has soft deletes (`deleted` boolean column) — deleted records are never hard-deleted
- PowerSync handles reactive queries — do NOT build custom refresh/watch patterns
